/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  conventions/Edwards-Hkgatm-v1.dat -- a VERSIONED, IMMUTABLE convention
  profile (equilibrium-parameterisation identity ADR, ratified 2026-07-26).

  The convention of Edwards, Maurer, Newman & Prausnitz, AIChE J. 24(6):
  966-976 (1978) for the Henry constants of volatile weak electrolytes in
  water -- Table 3 / Eq 13.  It is NOT the Sander-Hxp-v1 convention and the
  two must never be mixed in one calculation:

    * the composition basis is MOLALITY, not liquid mole fraction, so
      Edwards' H has units of kg-atm/mol.  Its numerical value differs from
      an H_xp by the factor 1/M_w (about 55.5) plus the activity
      convention;
    * the reference pressure is the SATURATION PRESSURE OF WATER at the
      system temperature, P_w^s -- not 1 atm.  H is tabulated at P_w^s and
      carried to the system pressure by the Krichevsky-Kasarnovsky term of
      Eq 11,  ln H^(P) = ln H^(P_w^s) + vbar_a^inf (P - P_w^s)/(R T),
      with the infinite-dilution partial molar volumes of Table 2;
    * the temperature form is Eq 13, ln H = B1/T + B2 ln T + B3 T + B4,
      with T in KELVIN (the paper quotes ranges of validity in degC but
      writes every correlation in K);
    * the solute activity coefficient is the UNSYMMETRIC gamma* of Eq 8
      (Pitzer truncation, Edwards parameterisation), normalised to unity at
      infinite dilution -- so an H from this profile is only meaningful
      alongside `activityModel edwardsPitzer`.

  THIS PROFILE DOES NOT REPLACE Sander-Hxp-v1 FOR THE SAME PAIR.  The D2
  identity contract makes a parameterisation the unit of identity: NH3-water
  under Sander and NH3-water under Edwards are two curated records that
  coexist, each naming its own convention, and a case selects one.  Neither
  is "the" Henry constant for ammonia.

  Once published this profile NEVER changes -- corrections mint a -v2.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType    conventionProfile;
schemaVersion 1;

name                 Edwards-Hkgatm-v1;
gasStandardState     idealGas;
compositionBasis     molality;
referencePressure    waterSaturation;
pressureCorrection   KrichevskyKasarnovsky;
temperatureForm      EdwardsEq13;
soluteReference      infiniteDilutionUnsymmetric;
solventReference     pureLiquid;
requiredActivityModel edwardsPitzer;
source               "Edwards, Maurer, Newman & Prausnitz, AIChE J. 24(6):966-976 (1978), Table 3 / Eqs 11 and 13";
